{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "pw8-demo-lfo-wobble",
    "name": "DEMO: LFO WOBBLE",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "Modulation demo: a single fast LFO1 -> Filter Cutoff route, amount 36 semitones (LFO sources are bipolar -1..1, so this swings +/-3 octaves around a 700Hz center -- FilterCutoff's exponential 'cutoffHz *= 2^(sum/12)' semantics, ModMatrixExecutor.hpp). LFO1 runs at 4Hz triangle, the classic audible 'wobble bass' rate. A light Saturation adds grit so the sweep reads as bass movement, not just a filter demo in isolation. Everything else (envelope, reverb) stays deliberately plain so the wobble is the whole story.",
    "category": "bass",
    "moods": [
      "modulation-demo",
      "wobble",
      "aggressive"
    ],
    "genres": [
      "demo"
    ],
